  "docstring": "Suppose monotone sequence $A$ satisfies the following: `A 0 = 1` and for all `j`, `A (j + 1)` is the\nsmallest natural number that cannot be written as a sum of consecutive terms of `A 0, ..., A j`.\nThen it is conjectured that $$a_k ~ \\frac{k \\log k}{\\log \\log k}$$. ",
